    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Article 226 gives High Courts wider writ jurisdiction than the Supreme Court under Article 32, as it covers fundamental rights as well as ordinary legal rights.",
        "Article 215 establishes the High Court as a Court of Record with authority to punish for contempt.",
        "Article 227 grants power of superintendence over all courts and tribunals throughout the territories in relation to which it exercises jurisdiction."
      ],
